{"result": "{\n    \"title\": \"Cáncer y Nutrición\",\n    \"summary\": \"La comunidad se centra en la interrelación entre el cáncer y la nutrición, destacando la importancia de la atención nutricional en pacientes oncológicos. Las entidades clave incluyen el cáncer, la sonda de gastrostomía, la inmunonutrición enteral y diversos tipos de cáncer, todos los cuales están interconectados a través de la necesidad de soporte nutricional y el impacto de la dieta en la progresión de la enfermedad.\",\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"La calificación de severidad de impacto es alta debido a la prevalencia del cáncer y su relación crítica con la nutrición, que afecta directamente la calidad de vida y los resultados del tratamiento de los pacientes.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"La malnutrición es común en pacientes con cáncer\",\n            \"explanation\": \"La malnutrición relacionada con el cáncer es un problema significativo que afecta a muchos pacientes, complicando su tratamiento y recuperación. Esta condición puede surgir debido a cambios metabólicos, efectos secundarios del tratamiento y reducción de la ingesta de alimentos. La malnutrición no solo afecta la eficacia del tratamiento, sino que también puede ser un factor de riesgo en el desarrollo del cáncer, lo que subraya la necesidad de intervenciones nutricionales adecuadas para mejorar la salud y los resultados de los pacientes [Data: Relaciones (699, 932, 7036, 19500, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"La sonda de gastrostomía es crucial para la nutrición enteral\",\n            \"explanation\": \"La sonda de gastrostomía es un dispositivo médico esencial para proporcionar soporte nutricional a largo plazo a pacientes que no pueden alimentarse por vía oral. Este dispositivo permite la nutrición enteral, facilitando la alimentación directa en el estómago, lo que es vital para mantener el estado nutricional en pacientes oncológicos que enfrentan dificultades para comer. La utilización de la sonda de gastrostomía es especialmente relevante en el contexto de la atención a pacientes con cáncer, donde la nutrición adecuada es fundamental para el manejo de la enfermedad [Data: Relaciones (3413, 2706, 7000, 3724, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"La inmunonutrición enteral mejora la respuesta inmune\",\n            \"explanation\": \"La inmunonutrición enteral se asocia con beneficios en la respuesta inmune y la recuperación postoperatoria en pacientes con cáncer. Este tipo de nutrición está diseñado para mejorar la salud general del paciente y puede ser crucial en el tratamiento de cáncer, donde la respuesta inmune es vital para combatir la enfermedad. La implementación de la inmunonutrición puede ayudar a mitigar los efectos negativos del tratamiento y mejorar los resultados clínicos [Data: Relaciones (595, 4802, 7040, 18457, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"La dieta mediterránea puede reducir el riesgo de cáncer\",\n            \"explanation\": \"La dieta mediterránea ha mostrado promesas en la reducción del riesgo de varios tipos de cáncer, incluyendo el cáncer colorrectal y de mama. Esta dieta, rica en frutas, verduras, granos enteros y ácidos grasos omega-3, se asocia con beneficios para la salud que pueden influir positivamente en la prevención del cáncer. La adopción de hábitos alimenticios saludables es fundamental para la prevención y el manejo del cáncer, destacando la importancia de la nutrición en la salud pública [Data: Relaciones (7034, 7303, 7309, 7300, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"El consumo de carne roja y procesada está relacionado con un mayor riesgo de cáncer\",\n            \"explanation\": \"El consumo de carne roja y procesada se ha vinculado a un aumento del riesgo de varios tipos de cáncer, incluyendo el cáncer colorrectal y gástrico. Estos hallazgos resaltan la importancia de las elecciones dietéticas en la prevención del cáncer y sugieren que la reducción de la ingesta de estos tipos de carne podría ser beneficiosa para la salud. La investigación en este ámbito es crucial para desarrollar pautas dietéticas que ayuden a mitigar el riesgo de cáncer [Data: Relaciones (7011, 7012, 7308, 7307, +more)].\"\n        }\n    ]\n}", "input": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery. Information discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims. The report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact. The content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their legal compliance, technical capabilities, reputation, and noteworthy claims.\n\n# Report Structure\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {{\n        \"title\": <report_title>,\n        \"summary\": <executive_summary>,\n        \"rating\": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": <rating_explanation>,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n1645,CÁNCER,\"CÁNCER is a complex group of diseases characterized by the uncontrolled growth of abnormal cells in the body. This condition can lead to significant health complications, including malnutrition and weight loss, as it often affects the metabolism and nutrient intake of patients. The disease is associated with various treatment modalities such as surgery, chemotherapy, radiotherapy, and immunotherapy, all of which can further complicate nutritional status and require specialized nutritional support.\n\nPatients with cancer frequently experience increased metabolic needs and may suffer from anorexia, necessitating enteral nutrition to maintain health and manage treatment side effects. The nutritional challenges faced by cancer patients can lead to deficits and metabolic alterations that impact their quality of life. Therefore, careful dietary management is essential, and certain dietary factors, including the consumption of fruits, vegetables, and omega-3 fatty acids, have been studied for their potential influence on cancer risk and progression.\n\nResearch indicates that dietary habits and lifestyle choices play a significant role in cancer risk, with associations found between cancer and the consumption of red and processed meats, as well as salt and dairy products. Conversely, adherence to a Mediterranean diet has shown promise in reducing the risk of several types of cancer, including colorectal and breast cancer.\n\nCÁNCER is a major global health issue, contributing to high morbidity and mortality rates. It is crucial for healthcare providers to address the nutritional needs of cancer patients, as proper dietary support can enhance treatment outcomes and overall well-being. The disease is also a focus of extensive research, with various thematic networks dedicated to advancing understanding and treatment of cancer through cooperative projects.\",66\r\n4871,SONDA DE GASTROSTOMÍA,\"The \"\"SONDA DE GASTROSTOMÍA\"\" is a medical device designed to provide long-term nutritional support for patients who are unable to eat orally. It is inserted into the stomach through the abdominal wall, facilitating enteral nutrition. This device is particularly useful in procedures such as endoscopic gastrostomy, where it allows for direct feeding into the stomach. The gastrostomy tube can be replaced by a button once a gastrocutaneous fistula has formed, offering a more comfortable option for ongoing nutritional support. Overall, the gastrostomy tube is essential for patients who cannot maintain adequate nutritional status through oral intake.\",8\r\n13396,INMUNONUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,La inmunonutrición enteral es un tipo de nutrición que se asocia con beneficios en la respuesta inmune y la recuperación postoperatoria en pacientes con cáncer.,4\r\n5924,CÁNCER COLORRECTAL,\"Cáncer colorrectal, or colorectal cancer, is a type of cancer that affects the colon and rectum. Its incidence has been linked to various dietary factors and lifestyle choices. Research indicates that the consumption of legumes may reduce the risk of developing adenomas and carcinomas associated with this cancer. Additionally, a higher intake of dietary fiber and whole grains has been shown to lower the risk of colorectal cancer, suggesting that fiber plays a protective role through various proposed mechanisms.\n\nObesity is identified as a contributing risk factor for colorectal cancer, highlighting the importance of maintaining a healthy weight. Furthermore, the consumption of omega-3 fatty acids has also been associated with a reduced risk of this disease. Conversely, a high intake of red and processed meats has been linked to an increased risk of colorectal adenomas, emphasizing the negative impact of certain dietary choices.\n\nThe relationship between colorectal cancer and the consumption of fruits and vegetables is noted to be inversely related, although the evidence supporting this connection is considered modest. Overall, dietary habits, including the intake of fiber, legumes, and omega-3 fatty acids, alongside lifestyle factors such as obesity, play significant roles in the risk of developing cáncer colorrectal.\",9\r\n7300,DIETA RICA EN FRUTAS Y VERDURAS,Una dieta que incluye un alto consumo de frutas y verduras se asocia con una reducción del riesgo de varios tipos de cáncer.,8\r\n7303,CÁNCER HEPÁTICO,\"Cáncer hepático is a type of liver cancer that has been the subject of various studies, particularly concerning its relationship with dietary factors. Research indicates that a high intake of omega-3 fatty acids may have implications for the risk of developing this cancer. Additionally, a significant inverse association has been observed between fish consumption and the risk of cáncer hepático, suggesting that higher fish intake may lower the likelihood of this disease. Furthermore, the consumption of white meat has been noted to potentially reduce the risk of cáncer hepático. In contrast, an increase in the intake of vegetables has also been linked to a decreased risk of developing this type of cancer. Overall, dietary choices, including the consumption of fish, white meat, and vegetables, play a crucial role in influencing the risk of cáncer hepático.\",4\r\n7308,CARNE PROCESADA,\"La carne procesada se relaciona con un incremento del riesgo de cáncer colorrectal, páncreas, y otros tipos de cáncer.\",2\r\n7307,CARNE ROJA,\"La carne roja se asocia con un aumento del riesgo de varios tipos de cáncer, incluyendo cáncer esofágico, gástrico y colorrectal.\",2\r\n7299,CRUCÍFERAS,Las verduras crucíferas son un grupo de vegetales que han sido objeto de investigación por sus potenciales efectos protectores frente al cáncer.,2\r\n7310,CÁNCER DE VEJIGA,\"Cáncer de vejiga is a type of bladder cancer that has been studied for its associations with dietary factors, particularly omega-3 intake. Research indicates that higher consumption of red and processed meats, as well as nitrites, is linked to an increased risk of developing cáncer de vejiga.\",2\r\n13360,MALNUTRICIÓN RELACIONADA CON EL CÁNCER,\"Malnutrition related to cancer refers to the nutritional deficiencies that occur in patients due to the disease and its treatment, impacting their overall health.\",2\r\n13616,NUPAC,\"NUPAC is a study focused on the nutritional assessment of cancer patients, highlighting the prevalence of malnutrition in this population.\",2\r\n7309,NITRITOS,Los nitritos presentes en la carne están asociados con un mayor riesgo de cáncer gástrico y de vejiga.,1\r\n7325,PERSONAS DE MEDIANA EDAD,,1\r\n7323,CÁNCER DE PULMÓN EN MUJERES,\"Tipo específico de cáncer de pulmón que puede verse influenciado por el consumo de ácidos grasos omega-3, con un posible efecto protector en mujeres.\",1\r\n7324,CÁNCER DE MAMA EN MUJERES,\"Tipo de cáncer que afecta a las mujeres y que puede ser influenciado por la ingesta de ácidos grasos omega-3, mostrando una reducción en el riesgo con la suplementación.\",1\r\n7335,LACTOFERRINA,\"Lactoferrin is a component of milk that exhibits antioxidant and anti-inflammatory properties, potentially inhibiting cell proliferation.\",1\r\n13361,GRUPO ERAS,El grupo ERAS (Enhanced Recovery After Surgery) proporciona recomendaciones para la recuperación de pacientes con tumores digestivos.,1\r\n15437,BOTÓN DE GASTROSTOMÍA,El botón de gastrostomía es un dispositivo que permite la colocación de una válvula unidireccional en el punto de inserción de la gastrostomía.,1\r\n13617,VSG-PG,\"VSG-PG (Valoración Subjetiva Global Generada por el Paciente) is a subjective global assessment tool used to evaluate the nutritional status of patients, particularly in oncology.\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3096,PACIENTE,CÁNCER,\"The entity \"\"PACIENTE\"\" refers to individuals who are diagnosed with \"\"CÁNCER.\"\" These patients often face a range of challenges associated with their condition, including complications such as malnutrition and caquexia. The effects of cancer and its treatment can significantly impact their nutritional status, necessitating specialized nutritional support to address these issues. Overall, patients with cancer require comprehensive care that considers their unique nutritional needs and the symptoms they may experience.\",612\r\n3413,PACIENTE,SONDA DE GASTROSTOMÍA,Se colocó una sonda de gastrostomía en el paciente para facilitar la nutrición enteral.,554\r\n4802,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CÁNCER,La nutrición parenteral es necesaria para pacientes con cáncer que tienen insuficiencia intestinal grave,504\r\n2774,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,CÁNCER,La nutrición enteral se utiliza para estabilizar el estado nutricional de pacientes con cáncer que no pueden ingerir alimentos por vía oral,401\r\n2706,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,SONDA DE GASTROSTOMÍA,\"La sonda de gastrostomía es otra opción para la nutrición enteral del paciente, utilizada cuando la sonda de gastroyeyunostomía no es efectiva\",343\r\n596,PACIENTES,CÁNCER,\"The entity \"\"PACIENTES\"\" refers to individuals who are diagnosed with \"\"CÁNCER\"\" and are in need of nutritional treatment. These patients often suffer from anorexia, a common symptom associated with cancer, which can lead to difficulties in maintaining adequate nutrition. As a result, they may require enteral nutrition to support their dietary needs during treatment.\",293\r\n801,NUTRICIÓN,CÁNCER,\"NUTRICIÓN and CÁNCER are closely interconnected, as cancer significantly impacts nutrition, making it a critical factor in the treatment and management of cancer patients. The nutritional intervention is essential to mitigate the effects of cancer on the patient's health, highlighting the importance of addressing dietary needs and nutritional support in cancer care.\",275\r\n595,PACIENTES,INMUNONUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,Los pacientes son los receptores de la inmunonutrición enteral durante su tratamiento,231\r\n1567,DIABETES MELLITUS,CÁNCER,La diabetes mellitus es un factor de riesgo que puede complicar la malnutrición en pacientes con cáncer,230\r\n6997,CÁNCER,MALNUTRICIÓN,\"Cancer and malnutrition are closely interconnected, with malnutrition being a prevalent issue among cancer patients. This condition arises due to various factors associated with the disease, including metabolic changes, treatment side effects, and reduced food intake. Malnutrition not only complicates the treatment and recovery of cancer patients but also significantly impacts patient outcomes and the overall efficacy of cancer therapies. Furthermore, malnutrition can serve as a risk factor in the development of cancer, highlighting the importance of addressing nutritional needs in cancer care to improve patient health and treatment success.\",170\r\n6760,NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL,CÁNCER,\"NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL is a treatment indicated for cancer patients who are unable to adequately nourish themselves due to the effects of their condition or its treatment. Cancer patients often require nutritional support to manage the side effects of their treatment, making artificial nutrition an essential component of their care. This approach helps ensure that patients receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery during a challenging time.\",159\r\n7029,CÁNCER,CALCIO,\"Calcium from dietary sources, particularly dairy, is inversely associated with digestive cancers.\",149\r\n1755,SARCOPENIA,CÁNCER,\"El sedentarismo en pacientes con cáncer puede provocar sarcopenia, afectando negativamente su estado físico\",149\r\n3724,NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT,SONDA DE GASTROSTOMÍA,Nutritional support may involve the use of a gastrostomy tube for long-term feeding in patients unable to eat orally,141\r\n932,DESNUTRICIÓN,CÁNCER,\"Desnutrición is a common consequence of cáncer, significantly impacting both the efficacy of treatment and the overall quality of life for patients. This condition is particularly prevalent among individuals with advanced stages of cáncer, highlighting the critical need for nutritional support in this population to improve health outcomes.\",140\r\n7034,CÁNCER,DIETA MEDITERRÁNEA,La dieta mediterránea se asocia con una disminución del riesgo de varios tipos de cáncer.,125\r\n8069,OBESITY,CÁNCER COLORRECTAL,Obesity is associated with an increased risk of colorectal cancer,125\r\n7038,CÁNCER,PROTEÍNAS,La ingesta adecuada de proteínas es crucial para pacientes con cáncer para mantener un balance nitrogenado positivo,123\r\n6872,INSUFICIENCIA RENAL,CÁNCER,La insuficiencia renal afecta las recomendaciones de ingesta proteica en pacientes con cáncer,107\r\n7005,CÁNCER,ALCOHOL,El consumo de alcohol ha demostrado ser un factor de riesgo para el desarrollo de cáncer.,93\r\n3625,PÉRDIDA DE PESO,CÁNCER,Cáncer often leads to pérdida de peso as a significant symptom due to various factors including tumor presence and treatment effects.,93\r\n7006,CÁNCER,FIBRA,\"CÁNCER and FIBRA are interconnected through the impact of dietary fiber on health outcomes. Research indicates that an increase in fiber intake is associated with a decrease in cardiovascular mortality and may also influence cancer risk. Specifically, high fiber consumption has been linked to a reduced risk of certain types of cancer. This suggests that incorporating more fiber into the diet could be beneficial for both cardiovascular health and cancer prevention.\",91\r\n7002,CÁNCER,CAQUEXIA,\"Cachexia is a condition frequently associated with cancer, resulting in significant weight loss and malnutrition among affected patients. It is a serious complication that contributes to the overall decline in health and quality of life for individuals suffering from cancer. In Spanish, it is noted that \"\"la caquexia es una condición que se presenta en pacientes con cáncer y contribuye a la malnutrición,\"\" emphasizing its role in exacerbating malnutrition in these patients.\",90\r\n7033,CÁNCER,VLCD,El cáncer es una contraindicación para el uso de dietas VLCD,90\r\n895,QUIMIOTERAPIA,CÁNCER,\"Quimioterapia is a common treatment method for cancer, aimed at reducing or eliminating cancerous cells\",89\r\n7015,CÁNCER,CÁNCER GÁSTRICO,El cáncer gástrico se relaciona con el alto consumo de nitritos de la carne roja o procesada.,88\r\n6996,CÁNCER,TUMOR,\"Cáncer is characterized by the presence of tumors, which can lead to various symptoms including weight loss.\",87\r\n6998,CÁNCER,DHA,Research indicates that DHA may play a role in suppressing cancer development,85\r\n6999,CÁNCER,EPA,\"CÁNCER and EPA are interconnected in the context of health and nutrition. The Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) plays a crucial role in assessing the impact of nutrition on health, particularly concerning diseases such as cancer. Research indicates that EPA may have beneficial effects that could aid in the prevention of cancer, highlighting the importance of understanding the relationship between environmental factors, nutrition, a